Ricky, played by Johnny Lewis.

10
00:39:10,000 --> 00:39:16,000
Predator: Requiem (stylized on-screen as  AVPR: Aliens vs Predator - Requiem) is a 2007 American
science fiction action horror film that is the second installment in the Alien vs.

11
00:43:05,000 --> 00:43:11,000
Predator franchise, and a sequel to Alien vs.

12
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:06,000
Predator (2004).

13
00:50:55,000 --> 00:51:01,000
The film was directed by the Brothers Strause
from a screenplay by Shane Salerno.

14
00:54:50,000 --> 00:54:56,000
Set immediately after the events of the previous film, the film begins with a Predator ship crashing into a forest outside of
Gunnison, Colorado, where an Alien-Predator hybrid known as the Predalien escapes and makes its way to the nearby small town.

15
00:58:45,000 --> 00:58:51,000
Wolf, a skilled veteran "cleaner", is dispatched to kill the Predalien,
and the townspeople try to escape the ensuing carnage.

16
01:02:40,000 --> 01:02:46,000
The film stars Steven Pasquale, Reiko Aylesworth, John
Ortiz, Johnny Lewis and Ariel Gade.

17
01:06:35,000 --> 01:06:41,000
Predator: Requiem premiered on November 4, 2007, in Los Angeles.

18
01:10:30,000 --> 01:10:36,000
It was released theatrically on December 25 in the United States.

19
01:14:25,000 --> 01:14:31,000
The film received generally negative reviews from critics for its
poor lighting, editing, and lack of originality.

20
01:18:20,000 --> 01:18:26,000
It grossed $130.2 million worldwide against a production budget of $40 million.

21
01:22:15,000 --> 01:22:21,000
Plans for another sequel were abandoned, with further independent entries
in both franchises released in 2010 and 2012 respectively.

22
01:26:10,000 --> 01:26:16,000
The film explores themes of predator, hybrid, colorado, national guard, morgue.

23
01:30:05,000 --> 01:30:11,000
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and intense.
